Macdeath by William Quakespeare!" Victoria said.

49
00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:40.151
"I love Quakespeare!" Ben exclaimed.

50
00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:44.425
"My uncle has taken me to see a bunch of Quakespeare plays.

51
00:03:44.426 --> 00:03:49.998
My favorites are Romeo and Ghouliet and Midsummer Nightmare

52
00:03:49.999 --> 00:03:54.266
." But some of the other students didn't seem very

53
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.102
enthusiastic. The mummy looked up from rewrapping his

54
00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:01.684
arm. "Quakespeare? The language in his plays is too

55
00:04:01.685 --> 00:04:06.507
old-fashioned." "I was hoping for a musical," Jen said

56
00:04:06.508 --> 00:04:11.381
sadly. "And besides, there are a lot of superstitions around Macdeath

57
00:04:11.382 --> 00:04:14.071
. I don't think it's a good

58
00:04:14.072 --> 00:04:17.959
choice." Like Ben, the three witches behind Winnie were

59
00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:23.484
excited. One of them, a redhead named Sonia, tapped Winnie on the

60
00:04:23.485 --> 00:04:26.194
shoulder. "Sorry, Winnie," she said with a

61
00:04:26.195 --> 00:04:28.630
smirk. "But don't even bother to

62
00:04:28.631 --> 00:04:33.201
audition. My friends and I are going to get the three witch

63
00:04:33.202 --> 00:04:34.734
parts." Winnie

64
